  "section_notes": "S1 imposes rapid 24-hour reporting for all known overheating/fire events and 72-hour customer notice, with 30-day investigation reports. S2 keeps the 55°C test and customer disclosure of per-model results but removes any automatic 5% sales bar, leaving restrictions to regulator risk assessment. S3 requires new-unit shut-off from 2028 and a 6-year installed-base retrofit where feasible; S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months with regulator-approved equivalents; S5 makes 8/100k a notification/investigation trigger rather than a mandatory recall."
